# Cursor Rules for Team Foodseekers (RMIT Hackathon 2026)
# Read AGENT_RULES.md for the complete specification.

## 🛑 STANDBY LOCK: CHƯA CÓ ĐỀ THI (DO NOT CODE YET!)
Official challenge has NOT been released yet (scheduled for 9:30 AM Oct 22, 2026).
DO NOT generate new models, pipelines, or dummy solutions unprompted.
Your only job right now: Ask user identity, verify `.venv`, install missing requirements, and explain reference docs if asked. Wait for human confirmation that the official challenge is released before coding.

## MANDATORY STEP 0: WHO IS THE USER & ENVIRONMENT VERIFICATION?
Before generating any code or executing commands, ASK THE HUMAN USER:
"Hello! Before we begin, please confirm which Foodseekers team member you are:
1. Thiện Nhân (Lead / AI Integration & Submissions) -> Directory: /src/models/, Branch: dev-backend
2. Văn Nhân (Core Engineer / Kaggle Runtime & Pipeline) -> Directory: /src/pipeline/, Branch: dev-core
3. Anh Thư (Data Analyst / Preprocessing & Features) -> Directory: /src/features/, Branch: dev-data
4. Minh Ngọc (System Architect / Red Teaming & Docs) -> Directory: /src/attacks/, Branch: dev-system
Please reply with your name or number so I can activate the correct role."

MANDATORY FIRST ACTION: Check if dependencies are installed in `.venv`. If not, run:
`pip install -r requirements.txt` (includes torch, transformers, underthesea, langdetect, scikit-learn).

## CORE DIRECTIVES:
1. Target platform is Kaggle. Deliverables must be valid Kaggle Notebooks or submission.csv. Do not build web GUIs.
2. NEVER commit directly to `main`. Always work on your designated branch (`dev-*`).
3. NEVER touch or delete files outside your designated directory.
4. NEVER commit API keys or secrets to Git. Use environment variables or .env.
5. Keep requirements.txt updated whenever adding dependencies.
6. Check TEAM_CHAT.md before each task to see team status. After finishing any task, append a 1-line update in VIETNAMESE to TEAM_CHAT.md: `* [Agent X - Tên Bạn] (HH:MM): [Nội dung đã làm, file ở đâu]` and commit it.
7. Take notes & document modules: When writing reusable scripts, append an entry to /CODE_INDEX.md (path, input, output, usage). Before coding new logic, check /CODE_INDEX.md to reuse existing work and prevent duplicate code.
8. NEVER merge into `main`, never force-push, never rebase someone else's branch. Only the Team Lead merges. Push your own `dev-*` branch and report in TEAM_CHAT.md.
9. Python 3.10-3.13 only (3.14 breaks underthesea/sklearn-crfsuite). Work inside `.venv`. Confirm `git config user.email` is YOURS (repo-local) before the first commit.
